 HISTORY                                                          3035 1451
 -------                                                          3035 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory (Mar   3035 1451
 2023) [1] using the FLASSH code [2].  The physical model is      3035 1451
 based on a mixed elastic scattering treatment and includes       3035 1451
 coherent elastic scattering, incoherent elastic scattering and   3035 1451
 inelastic scattering components.  This evaluation is intended    3035 1451
 to be used with the companion 7Li(7LiD) TSL evaluation when      3035 1451
 modeling enriched 7LiD.                                          3035 1451
                                                                  3035 1451
 THEORY                                                           3035 1451
 ------                                                           3035 1451
 Lithium hydride (LiD) has a fluorite (NaCl) type face-centered   3035 1451
 cubic crystal structure with four Li and D atoms per unit call.  3035 1451
 The inelastic scattering cross sections were calculated in the   3035 1451
 incoherent approximations using the D partial phonon density of  3035 1451
 states from a VASP/PHONON calculation of 7LiD.  The LiD crystal  3035 1451
 structure and lattice constant from [3] were used in the         3035 1451
 VASP/PHONON calculation.  The mixed elastic scattering           3035 1451
 treatment was used to account for both coherent and incoherent   3035 1451
 elastic scattering effects present in this material.  The        3035 1451
 coherent elastic scattering component was calculated in the      3035 1451
 cubic approximation using the FLASSH generalized coherent        3035 1451
 elastic scattering module using the 7LiD crystal structure and   3035 1451
 measured room temperature lattice constant of 4.0684 Ang [3]     3035 1451
 along with free atom coherent scattering cross sections of       3035 1451
 2.483 b for D from [4] and 0.51 b for Li-7 from [5]. The         3035 1451
 incoherent elastic scattering component was calculated using     3035 1451
 the Debye-Waller factor derived from the D partial phonon        3035 1451
 density of states and an D free atom incoherent scattering       3035 1451
 cross section of 0.912 b.  A D free atom total scattering cross  3035 1451
 section of 3.395 b was used for consistency with the             3035 1451
 ENDF/B-VIII.1 D evaluation. A phonon order of 500 was used to    3035 1451
 ensure both the inelastic scattering cross section and the       3035 1451
 S(alpha,beta) functions at elevated temperatures were            3035 1451
 adaquately converged.                                            3035 1451
